# Task 2 - Automated EBS Snapshot Creation and Cleanup

## Objective

Automate EBS volume backup creation and delete snapshots older than 30 days.

## AWS Services Used

- AWS Lambda
- Amazon EC2
- Amazon EBS
- Amazon EventBridge
- IAM
- Amazon CloudWatch

## Features

- Creates a snapshot of the specified EBS volume.
- Tags the snapshot with `CreatedBy=Lambda-Backup`.
- Lists snapshots created by the Lambda function.
- Deletes snapshots older than 30 days.
- Logs the IDs of created and deleted snapshots.

## Testing

The Lambda function was manually triggered. A new snapshot was successfully created and tagged. Older snapshots matching the retention policy were deleted. Snapshot creation and cleanup were verified in the EC2 console.

## Scheduling

The Lambda function can be scheduled using Amazon EventBridge to run weekly and automate backup management.

## Production Note

AWS Data Lifecycle Manager (DLM) is the preferred solution for standard snapshot scheduling and retention because it is fully managed.

AWS Lambda is useful when custom retention rules, cross-account snapshot copies, notifications, or additional automation steps are required.
